## 📚 Data Sources (public only)

| Source | Used for | Licence / terms |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| [OpenPhish Community Feed](https://openphish.com/) | Live phishing URLs | [Terms](https://openphish.com/terms.html) |
| [Phishing.Database](https://github.com/mitchellkrogza/Phishing.Database) | Active phishing URLs | See repository |
| [Phishing Army](https://phishing.army/) | Phishing domains | [Licence](https://phishing.army/license/) |
| [HaGeZi DNS Blocklists](https://github.com/hagezi/dns-blocklists) (Threat Intelligence Feeds, Gambling, Anti-Piracy) | Malware/scam, gambling, piracy domains | GPL-3.0 |
| [The Block List Project](https://github.com/blocklistproject/Lists) | Gambling, piracy, scam, malware domains | Unlicense |
| [Citizen Lab test list (Malaysia)](https://github.com/citizenlab/test-lists/blob/master/lists/my.csv) | Malaysian gambling sites (GMB) | CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 |
| [Tranco list](https://tranco-list.eu/) (incl. subdomains) | Legitimate / popular domains | Free for research (Le Pochat et al., NDSS 2019) |
| `url_dataset_synthetic.csv` | Malaysian-brand phishing patterns and long legitimate URLs (generated) | This project |

The feeds are handled as **text only**; the system never visits the listed sites. `fetch_threat_intel.py` re-downloads the latest versions. URLhaus (abuse.ch) malware URLs can be added with a free Auth-Key.

