## 🚀 Getting Started (Installation & Setup)

Follow these steps to set up and run the project on a new machine (PC or Laptop):

### 1. Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/SME-CyberSentry.git
cd SME-CyberSentry
```

### 2. Create and Activate the Python Virtual Environment
```powershell
# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate on Windows PowerShell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned
venv\Scripts\activate
```

### 3. Install Dependencies
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 4. Initialize the SQLite Database & Import the Datasets
```bash
python database/init_db.py              # schema + hand-curated Threat Dictionary
python backend/fetch_threat_intel.py    # downloads public feeds -> threat_intel.db (~280 MB) + url_dataset_public.csv
python backend/build_url_dataset.py     # Malaysian synthetic supplement -> url_dataset_synthetic.csv
python database/import_datasets.py      # loads ALL CSVs into the DB + mines dictionary phrases
```

### 5. Train the Models (Optional if `.pkl` files are already present)
```bash
python backend/train_model.py         # trains from the database; prints evaluation report
```

### 6. Start the Local Classification Engine
```bash
python backend/app.py
```
The local engine will start running at `http://127.0.0.1:5000`. Keep this terminal window open while using the browser extension.

### 7. Load the Chrome Browser Extension
1. Open Google Chrome and navigate to `chrome://extensions/`.
2. Enable **Developer mode** (toggle switch in the top-right corner).
3. Click **Load unpacked** (top-left button) and select the `extension/` folder inside this project.
4. Pin **SME-CyberSentry** to your Chrome toolbar.

